<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean du Plessis d'Ossonville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1635</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean du Plessis d'Ossonville was a French nobleman who, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-lienard-de-lolive">Charles Liénard de l'Olive</a>, led the colonists sent by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compagnie-des-iles-de-lamerique">Compagnie des Îles de l'Amérique</a> to settle Guadeloupe in June 1635. The expedition landed in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basse-terre">Basse-Terre</a> island, where the settlers suffered from hunger and fever. Du Plessis died later in 1635, leaving l'Olive in charge of the colony.</p></div>
